WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:07.049
Speaker 1: The Supreme Court on Friday dealt
another defeat to President Joe Biden blocking

00:00:07.049 --> 00:00:12.380
his student loan forgiveness program, CNN
reports.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:18.410
In a stinging defeat for President Joe Biden,
the Supreme Court blocked the administration

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:23.980
student loan forgiveness plan Friday, rejecting
a program aimed at delivering up to $20,000

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.420
of relief to millions of borrowers struggling
with outstanding debt.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.190
The decision was six three.

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:35.160
Chief Justice John Roberts wrote for the Conservative
Supermajority.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.700
This will become an issue in 2024.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.270
Biden can try to galvanize liberals by claiming
the conservative court prevented him from

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.700
delivering debt relief to voters.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.140
Republicans are celebrating the ruling as
a defeat for a bailout plan.

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:55.030
Republican led states and conservatives challenging
the program say it's an unlawful attempt to

00:00:55.030 --> 00:01:01.640
erase an estimated $430 billion of federal
student loan debt under the guise of the pandemic.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.450
Roberts said the Biden administration and
Secretary of Education rewrote the law that

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.150
it cannot fairly be called a waiver.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:15.330
It not only nullifies existing provisions,
but augments and expands them dramatically.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.250
However broad the meaning of waive or modify
that language cannot authorize the kind of

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.579
exhaustive rewriting of the statute that has
taken place here.

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:26.130
I have to tell you, this is not surprising.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:29.020
Every time we we talked about this, for example,
on the bonus.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.430
Speaker 2: Show, a David Pac-Man membership
because six bucks a month.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.430
Speaker 1: Yeah.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.090
Pat and I both said.

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.740
This is shaky.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:44.500
While we agree with the policy, this legal
basis is shaky and people would call in during

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.700
live calls and say, David, should I stop paying
my student loans?

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.740
I owe nine grand.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:55.080
Should I stop paying them because it might
all get paid off.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.360
And I said, don't take that advice from me.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.159
It's not obvious to me that this is going
to survive.

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:06.399
And it's not obvious to me that it makes sense
to allow interest to continue accumulating

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:09.300
while you wait for this to work its way through
the courts.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:11.420
And indeed, this was the decision.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:17.520
So, listen, the Supreme Court has handed Joe
Biden a number of defeats by now.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:25.630
The most important the most important takeaway
and realization from all of this is.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:31.210
None of this would be happening if Hillary
Clinton had defeated Donald Trump in 2016.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.010
And I know that there are people in my audience
who don't want to hear this.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:40.409
There are people who stayed home or voted
someone in or whatever in 2016 under the guise

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:43.610
that Hillary is just too conservative for
me.

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:44.610
Yeah, okay.

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.879
Trump's a clown, but not that different from
Hillary Clinton.

00:02:48.879 --> 00:02:53.489
And there were people like me and others who
were saying, That's really dangerous.

00:02:53.489 --> 00:02:58.620
We're not just pretending that the Supreme
Court issue could be a major issue.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.000
It really could.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Look.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:04.819
Now, Roe v Wade student loans.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.600
I can't even give you the full list.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.940
Most of this stuff doesn't happen if Hillary
Clinton wins in 2016.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:21.310
With rumors now of potentially multiple retirements
in the Supreme Court upcoming, I am going

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:29.610
to restate again and again that the Supreme
Court could be a major issue in the next presidential

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.080
term.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.439
And it is really important that we remember
that.

00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:36.750
And we take 2016 as a lesson as far as that
goes.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.040
So this is the Supreme Court's decision.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:42.140
This is a loss for Joe Biden.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:50.189
It is not a massive surprise, but it is a
reminder about the importance of the Supreme

00:03:50.189 --> 00:03:51.189
Court.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:52.189
And we've got a horrible Supreme Court right
now.

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:53.689
I mean, it's the reality.

00:03:53.689 --> 00:03:55.569
We have a horrible Supreme Court.

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:56.939
We will continue following it.

00:03:56.939 --> 00:04:01.739
We will see what other venues there may be,
if any, for Joe Biden to do student loan forgiveness.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:02.739
There are.

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:04.849
He could have done it with a different legal
justification.

00:04:04.849 --> 00:04:05.849
We've talked about it before.

00:04:05.849 --> 00:04:07.300
We will talk about it again.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:05:15.420
But that is the Supreme Court's decision.

